# Files the Vercel CLI must never upload.
#
# `.env` is gitignored, so it never reaches GitHub — but `vercel deploy` uploads
# the working directory independently of git and injects dotenv files as
# build-time environment variables. That silently baked the local
# `VITE_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318` into the production bundle, so every
# visitor's browser tried to export telemetry to their own machine and the UI
# reported "awaiting export" instead of the honest "OTLP off".
#
# A deployment built from Git would not have hit this, because a fresh checkout
# has no `.env`. Excluding it here makes the local path behave the same way.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Not needed to build, and large.
node_modules
dist
.vercel
.git
